{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QuantumObservableUniverses.QLogarithmExists","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QuantumObservableUniverses.QLogarithmExists","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Polynomial.Laurent"],"declarations":11,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QLogarithm.exists_in_shuffle_hopf","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QLogarithm.exists_in_shuffle_hopf","kind":"theorem","line":55,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/q-logarithm-exists.lean#L55-L82","doc":"**Existence of the q-logarithm primitive.**\n\nUnder the hypotheses of `QExponential.exists_in_shuffle_hopf`,\nthe q-shuffle Hopf algebra admits a primitive element `log_q`\nforming an adjoint pair with the q-exponential grouplike.\n\nThe construction uses Milnor–Moore to identify\nPrim(𝓗_q) with the Lie algebra of G(𝓗_q), then takes the\nformal inverse of exp_q. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:prop:q-logarithm-exists","label":"prop:q-logarithm-exists","md":"quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/q-logarithm-exists.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QLogarithm.counit_eq_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QLogarithm.counit_eq_zero","kind":"theorem","line":53,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/q-logarithm-exists.lean#L53-L53","doc":"Vanishing counit: ε(log_q) = 0. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QLogarithm.primitive_right","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QLogarithm.primitive_right","kind":"theorem","line":51,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/q-logarithm-exists.lean#L51-L51","doc":"Primitivity (right component): the second leg is `log_q`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QLogarithm.primitive_left","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QLogarithm.primitive_left","kind":"theorem","line":49,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/q-logarithm-exists.lean#L49-L49","doc":"Primitivity (left component): the first leg of\nΔ_q(log_q) = log_q ⊗ 1 + 1 ⊗ log_q is `log_q`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QLogarithm.one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QLogarithm.one","kind":"def","line":46,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/q-logarithm-exists.lean#L46-L46","doc":"The unit / grouplike `1 ∈ H` against which primitivity is taken. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QLogarithm.counit","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QLogarithm.counit","kind":"def","line":44,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/q-logarithm-exists.lean#L44-L44","doc":"Counit on H. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QLogarithm.coprod","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QLogarithm.coprod","kind":"def","line":42,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/q-logarithm-exists.lean#L42-L42","doc":"Coproduct on H, encoded as `coprod : H → H × H`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QLogarithm.log_q","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QLogarithm.log_q","kind":"def","line":40,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/q-logarithm-exists.lean#L40-L40","doc":"The primitive element log_q ∈ H. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QLogarithm.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QLogarithm.mk","kind":"ctor","line":38,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/q-logarithm-exists.lean#L38-L38","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QLogarithm","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QLogarithm","kind":"structure","line":27,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/q-logarithm-exists.lean#L27-L53","doc":"**q-Logarithm data**: an abstract primitive element of the\nq-shuffle Hopf algebra, characterised by primitivity\n`Δ_q(log_q) = log_q ⊗ 1 + 1 ⊗ log_q` and vanishing counit\n`ε(log_q) = 0`.\n\nMirrors `QExponential` in the sibling existence proof\n(`q-exponential-exists.lean`); inlined here so this proposition's\nsibling compiles standalone (the existence proof needs the\nstructure in scope). The two `primitive_*` fields encode the two\ncomponents of the primitivity coproduct relation. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:def:q-logarithm","label":"def:q-logarithm","md":"quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/q-logarithm.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.R_q","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.R_q","kind":"def","line":25,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/q-logarithm-exists.lean#L25-L25","signatureChunk":0}]}